"10:20:16","deltaSeconds":-110}}},"historicalRank":{"fieldSizeRank":8,"finishersRank":7,"finishRateRank":90,"winningTimeRank":2,"winningTimeRankDir":2,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"menRecords":["overall"],"menPreviousRecord":{"time":"05:20:41","holder":"Leonid SHVETSOV","year":2007,"type":"overall"},"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1959,"mensWinner":"Trevor ALLEN","mensTime":"06:28:11"}},"narrative":"The 2016 Comrades Marathon was the 91st running of the race, run in the 'down' direction from Pietermaritzburg to Durban over 89.208 kms. The race was held on Sunday, 29 May. Conditions: Cool at start. Mild to warm sunshine throughout the day. Runners had 12 hours to complete the course.\n\nDavid GATEBE claimed the men's title in 05:18:19, ahead of Ludwick MAMABOLO (05:24:05) and Bongmusa MTHEMBU (05:26:39). Charne BOSMAN won the women's race in 06:25:55, followed by Caroline CHERRY (06:30:44).\n\nDavid GATEBE's 05:18:19 set a new course record, beating Leonid SHVETSOV's 05:20:41 from 2007. Charne BOSMAN's 06:25:55 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1959 (Trevor ALLEN, 06:28:11).\n\nFrom a field of 21,551 entries, 14,432 runners crossed the finish line (67.0% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 11,466 men and 2,965 women (20.5% female). The average finish time was 10:18:26.\n\nMedals awarded: 20 Gold, 16 Wally Hayward, 605 Silver, 2,249 Bill Rowan, 6,416 Bronze, 5,125 Vic Clapham. 3,894 runners (27.0%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Bianca CALDWELL in 14:14:53.\n\nThis edition featured the 2nd fastest winning time on record. Compared to the previous down run in 2014, the field was 6.1% larger.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 57% of the finishers, with 6,199 seniors (avg 10:07:36) and 8,232 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}